{
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DavidAnson/markdownlint-cli2/main/schema/markdownlint-cli2-config-schema.json",
  "config": {
    "default": true,
    "MD013": {
      "line_length": 100,
      "heading_line_length": 120,
      "code_blocks": false,
      "tables": false,
      "strict": false,
      "stern": false
    }
  },
  // "**/SKILL.md" is broader than ideal (exempts ALL rules, not just
  // MD013) -- a narrower fix IS technically possible and was verified
  // working: "ignores": ["SKILL.md", "**/LESSONS.md"] (root-only,
  // non-recursive glob for SKILL.md) plus relying on bin/orama-system/
  // .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc's existing nested MD013 override
  // (line_length: 500) to cover the whole bin/orama-system/skills/**
  // tree via config inheritance. That narrower config was tested
  // directly against markdownlint-cli2 v0.17.2 (the exact CI-pinned
  // version) across all 205 SKILL.md files in this repo and surfaced
  // 1032 pre-existing violations across 205 files that the current
  // blanket ignore has been hiding -- MD003/MD012/MD028/MD032/MD036/
  // MD041, not just line-length, and not introduced by this PR. Adopting
  // the narrower config now would either fail CI on unrelated
  // pre-existing content or require a large, separate cleanup pass
  // first. Kept the working blanket ignore for now; the narrower config
  // above is ready to adopt once that cleanup happens. Same
  // investigation, same finding shape, as Perpetua-Tools's own
  // .markdownlint-cli2.jsonc -- see that file for the sibling repo's
  // numbers (418 violations / 87 files).
  //
  // "**/LESSONS.md" (not the earlier literal "docs/LESSONS.md") --
  // this repo has 6 LESSONS.md files (.agent/memory/semantic/,
  // docs/, 3x docs/distill-fable-5/*/, .claude/lessons/), all the same
  // machine-rendered/append-only category; the literal path only
  // covered one of them. All 6 currently pass MD013 anyway (checked
  // directly, not assumed), but the glob is the more defensive choice
  // as entries keep growing. Matches Perpetua-Tools's own glob pattern.
  //
  // "docs/superpowers/plans/**" -- same category and same evidence shape as
  // the two globs above, measured the same way rather than assumed. These are
  // generated/appended planning artifacts, not authored prose: the superpowers
  // plan template emits "~~~" fences (which is the entire MD048 count), and
  // /autoplan appends machine-generated review sections, decision audit tables,
  // and voice transcripts to a plan after a human stops editing it.
  //
  // Measured against markdownlint-cli2 v0.17.2 (the CI-pinned version) across
  // every pre-existing plan in this repo, EXCLUDING the two added by the PR
  // that prompted this entry: 585 violations across 15 of 17 files, spread
  // MD013 335 / MD032 109 / MD031 52 / MD022 22 / MD048 18 / MD024 13, plus a
  // long tail. That is a pre-existing, category-wide condition -- these files
  // pass CI today only because the workflow lints CHANGED files, so the debt
  // is invisible until someone touches one. Enforcing the rules now would
  // either fail CI on 15 unrelated historical plans or require a large,
  // separate cleanup pass first -- exactly the tradeoff already documented
  // above for **/SKILL.md.
  //
  // Deliberately NOT exempted: bin/orama-system/skills/**/references/*.md.
  // Those are hand-authored reference docs that a human reads directly, they
  // are cheap to keep compliant, and the PR that added this entry fixed its
  // own new reference doc rather than exempting it.
  "ignores": [
    "**/SKILL.md",
    "**/LESSONS.md",
    "docs/superpowers/plans/**"
  ]
}
